{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `log_radon`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual likelihood accumulation `target += normal_lpdf(log_radon[n] | mu[n], sigma_y)` inside the loop with a single vectorized built-in sampling statement `log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y)` after `mu` is computed. This is a same-density rewrite because Stan's vectorized normal likelihood sums the elementwise normal log densities. All parameter priors were already explicit and occur before parameter use. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> J;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county_idx;
  vector[N] log_uppm;
  vector[N] floor_measure;
  vector[N] log_radon;
}
parameters {
  vector[J] alpha;
  vector[2] beta;
  real mu_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
}
model {
  vector[N] mu;
  vector[N] muj;

  sigma_alpha ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 1);
  mu_alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  beta ~ normal(0, 10);

  alpha ~ normal(mu_alpha, sigma_alpha);
  for (n in 1 : N) {
    muj[n] = alpha[county_idx[n]] + log_uppm[n] * beta[1];
    mu[n] = muj[n] + floor_measure[n] * beta[2];
  }
  log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":2,"N":1,"county_idx":[2],"floor_measure":[2.781302226706768],"log_radon":[4.97025926619108],"log_uppm":[2.9018354722795787]}","protected_variables":["log_radon"]}
